ridge_onboard: Hey CS/Platform  we've got a bizarre surge during key rotation. We rotate ephemeral keys every 60s across the fleet; when rotation hits, ~120 pods refresh at once and we see a spike of 429s and a few 401s to /v1/complete. Any fast fixes?

noah_cs: Oof, thanks for flagging. Are these ephemeral creds orchestrated by your infra (cron) or by the SDK? Also how many pods and what SDK/version?

ridge_onboard: SDK is node v1.4.0, k8s HPA set to 120 replicas. Rotation is done by our sidecar process that writes a new env var to pods (we trigger a rolling restart every minute during rotation window).

irene_se: That workflow explains it  rolling restarts + immediate prefetch==thrashing. Two safe quick mitigations: 1) stop triggering simultaneous restarts during rotation window (stagger or do a leader refresh), 2) upgrade SDK to 1.4.5 which supports client-side ephemeralCache and single-flight preflight.

oliver_platform: Short-term we can also enable a grace period on the token validation so previously-issued tokens remain accepted for ~30s after rotation to avoid immediate mass refresh. Would you like us to toggle that while you change rolling restart pattern?

ridge_onboard: Yes please toggle grace. Also any code changes on our end we can drop in today?

irene_se: Minimal changes: stop eager prefetch during restarts, rely on cached token for first few requests, and add a single-flight lock so only one process fetches a new token while others wait. Example snippet (conceptual):
```js
// pseudo
const cache = new TokenCache();
async function getToken(){
  if (cache.valid()) return cache.token;
  return await cache.singleFlightFetch(async ()=>{
     const t = await client.fetchEphemeral();
     cache.set(t);
     return t;
  });
}
```
Also set `keepAlive:true` and `maxConnections:10`.

noah_cs: Can you also tell us whether your sidecar deletes the old token immediately? If yes, consider keeping old token until new one is confirmed across pods. That avoids 401 cascades.

ridge_onboard: Yup sidecar deletes old token immediately. Well change that to a swap window.

ops-bot: preflight_coalesce flag enabled for tenant ridge_onboard until ts=1751115980.

tz-bot: grace-window feature toggled for tenant ridge_onboard: token_grace=30s until ts=1751115980.

ridge_onboard: After enabling grace-window and preflight_coalesce and changing sidecar to delay deletion, the 401s disappeared and 429s reduced significantly. We also added a 0-10s stagger to rolling restart so pods don't all init at once. Logs:```log
[1751112260] restart: pod/alpha-23 scheduled splay=7.3s
[1751112270] preflight: cache hit uid=rid token_age=15s
[1751112272] complete:200 latency=170ms
```

irene_se: Great. Follow-up suggestions for a durable fix: - Migrate to SDK >=1.4.5 for single-flight preflight and better caching - If you must rotate frequently, perform rotation via a central refresh service or leader election so only N pods refresh per interval - If using k8s, use rolling update strategy with maxUnavailable=1 to limit concurrent restarts - Add 429 backoff with jitter at request layer

noah_cs: I'll draft a short runbook and paste recommended flags: `ephemeralCache:true`, `preflightCoalesce:true`, `startupSplay=0-10s`, `token_swap_delay=30s`, `keepAlive:true`, `maxConnections=8`, `retry: {base:200ms, max:10s, jitter:true}`. Also include an Ops checklist to request permanent quota bump if you expect sustained simultaneous boots.

ridge_onboard: Sounds perfect. We'll schedule the SDK upgrade and change the sidecar to swap-with-delay. Please keep preflight_coalesce and grace-window on for 24h while we run a full rollout. Thanks all :raised_hands:

oliver_platform: Done  left both feature flags on for 24h and will monitor. Ping if you see any anomalies.

noah_cs: Added runbook link to onboarding checklist and will follow up with a postmortem template to capture rotation schedule, TTLs, and the root cause so renewal/health team can note risk.
